  "Specification": "This module is a test specification for the standard Bags module, defining a collection of concrete bag values and then asserting expected properties of the bag operators over those examples. It checks bag well-formedness, cardinality, membership, conversion between sets and bags, copy counts, bag addition and subtraction, bag union, subbag ordering, and BagOfAll mapping behavior, using many ASSUME statements as executable test assertions for TLC. The module ends with a trivial temporal specification `[][TRUE]_<<>>` only to make model checking run; it does not model a transition system with variables, faults, or nontrivial temporal behavior.",
